arm64: panic and exception hooks for boards (optional)

Adds two weak hooks, board_exception_hook(regs) and board_panic_hook(msg), called just before
U-Boot resets on an arm64 exception or a panic(). With them a board can save a record that
survives the reset; abboot's diagnostics (CONFIG_AB_CRUMBS) use them through
ab_crumbs_exception() and ab_crumbs_panic(). Not needed for anything else.

Against U-Boot v2026.10. SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later

diff --git a/arch/arm/lib/interrupts_64.c b/arch/arm/lib/interrupts_64.c
index b3024ba5..1bdfb121 100644
